With ticket OAK-11949 we introduced the feature that union queries are sorted by score, instead of simply concatenating them. However, turning on the feature toggle causes NullPointerExceptions in some rare cases. The problem occurs if there is a score column, but accessing a score of that column returns Null. This can happen if, for example, there is a union between three queries, of which at least one has scores, and at least one doesn't have, and those two results are merged first. 
{code:java}
